{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And I will give peace.</b> Lest you say: there is food and there is drink — if there is no peace, there is nothing — therefore Scripture says after all this: ״וְנָתַתִּי שָׁלוֹם בָּאָרֶץ״. From this: peace is weighed against everything, and so it says (Isaiah 45): ״עֹשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם וּבוֹרֵא אֶת הַכֹּל״." "<b>And the sword shall not pass through your land.</b> It is unnecessary to say that they will not come for war — but even to pass through your land from one province to another (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:35.287491458Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}